    "Single machine, single sitting (see `machine` block below) -- not a controlled lab, just a repeatable local measurement.",
    "nav_s is time-to-domcontentloaded, not full page load; some sites keep loading async resources after this point.",
    "cpu_s is total CPU time (user+system, summed across every process in the tree) consumed during the 2s sampling window after goto() returns -- not wall-clock time, so it can exceed 2s when multiple processes/cores are busy at once.",
    "rss_mb is the max RSS seen across the ~8 samples taken every 0.25s for 2s after goto() returns (true peak, not a single snapshot).",
    "rss_mb sums the whole process tree (Playwright's Node driver + all Chromium subprocesses), so it's not purely 'browser' memory -- but that overhead is identical in both modes, so the headless-vs-headful delta is still an apples-to-apples comparison."
